cmu-utility-drone-script-hint = One command per line or separated by spaces. Use braces for if/while/repeat blocks. Marker numbers are 1-based and taken from the Markers tab.
cmu-utility-drone-script-help = Values: marker(1), hand("left"), activehand(), equipped("back"), backpack(target), backpackitem("crowbar"), item("crowbar", 8), peoplecount(5), itemcount(8), backpackcount(), name(entity), itemname(entity), itemid(entity), itemdisplay("name", 8), handname("left"), inhand("right"), hasbackpackitem("crowbar"), distance(entity), damage(entity), pulling(entity), aimtarget(entity), hands(target), worn(target), backpacknames(target), backpackitems(target), nearestperson(8), peoplenames(8), inspectperson(target), worncontains(target, "wey"), exists(value), attacker(), damagetaken(), heardtext(), heardspeaker(), backpackfits(item), health(target), maxhealth(target), healthpercent(target), alive(target), dead(target), critical(target), nearesthostile(8), hostiles(8), hostilecount(8), nearestally(8), ammo(), maxammo(), incombat(). Arithmetic: + - * / %, comparisons, && || !. Flow: let x = 0, set x = x + 1, if, else, while, repeat, restart, stop.
cmu-utility-drone-script-action-help = Movement: move coords X Y, move up/down/left/right [distance]. Item use: use self, use on target, use item on target. Targets can be entities or names. Combat: wield [item], unwield, aim at target, aim coords X Y, shoot [count], shoot at target, reload, hold fire, free fire, fight [target] [within radius], disengage. Repair: repair [self|ally|target] [within radius]; repair refuses to work while hostiles are nearby. Labels use 'name:' and 'goto name'; handlers may use 'goto main.name', 'return', 'restart' or 'stop'.
cmu-utility-drone-script-info-help = World information for say: hands(), worn(), backpacknames(), backpackitems(), person("Urist"), people(8), items(8), entities(8). Example: say "People: " + people(8).
cmu-utility-drone-script-item-hint = take and pull accept an entity or an item name: take "crowbar", pull "crowbar", or pull item("crowbar", 8). Names match whole words.
cmu-utility-drone-script-event-hint = Event rules: on damaged runs even while the main program is moving or waiting. on heard "phrase" can interrupt the current task. Handlers can use any statements and actions; use return to resume main, goto main.label to switch tasks, restart to start main over, or stop to finish. damagetaken() polls the pending hit once, attacker() is the last attacker, and backpackfits(item) checks free space before put in backpack.
cmu-utility-drone-marker-script-hint = Script marker numbers use the order shown here: marker 1 is the first entry, marker 2 the second, and so on. The registry is frozen into the board when it is printed.
